  "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B013",
        "laureates": [
          "Marc Feldmann",
          "Ravinder N. Maini"
        ],
        "citation": "for establishing TNF blockade as a treatment for rheumatoid arthritis and inflammatory disease"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B022",
    "B045"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B013 most clearly joins a pathogenic cytokine insight to decisive clinical demonstration of a durable disease-modifying treatment principle. Its medical effects across inflammatory disease are mature, and Feldmann and Maini remain a focused proposed pair for the central mechanistic rationale and its clinical validation. The prize can be delimited to establishing TNF blockade, rather than crediting all subsequent anti-TNF products, indications, or implementation.",
    "case_against": "The anti-TNF field involved substantial wider academic, clinical, and industrial work, and a priority review remains necessary to establish whether the proposed pair captures all indispensable contributions. B013 also has a more focused mechanistic scope than B024 and less immediately broad population reach than B022 or B045.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson favors B022 for combining fundamental GLP-1 physiology with a broad, mature therapeutic transformation, while recognizing difficult boundaries among hormone biology, physiology, and drug development.",
        "response": "I agree that B022 has exceptional and well-established medical consequences. I retain B013 because its awardable mechanism-to-treatment pathway is more sharply bounded in the supplied evidence: TNF blockade can be distinguished from the later expansion of anti-TNF medicines, whereas the proposed B022 allocation still spans several distinct foundational and translational stages."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
        "point": "Perlmann favors B045 because vaccine-enabling HPV virus-like-particle work led to durable prevention of infection and related cancers, subject to careful separation from product development and implementation.",
        "response": "B045 is an outstanding alternative, especially for its preventive consequence. The same attribution discipline that Perlmann applies to HPV VLP work is decisive for both candidates. On the present record, B013 more directly identifies a compact mechanistic hypothesis and its clinical proof, while B045 still requires a fuller division among VLP work, papillomavirus biology, vaccine development, and implementation."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "sandberg-rickard",
        "point": "Sandberg favors B024 as a deeply validated, fundamental mechanism of endoplasmic-reticulum stress adaptation with compact proposed attribution to Mori and Walter.",
        "response": "B024's fundamental importance and concise attribution are substantial strengths. I continue to give greater weight to B013 because the evidence connects the cytokine mechanism to a long-established, disease-modifying therapeutic principle; B024's medical implications should not be assumed from its broad biological influence alone."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether detailed historical review confirms that Feldmann and Maini alone represent the indispensable conceptual and clinical contributions to establishing TNF blockade.",
      "Whether B022 can define an equally delimited awardable achievement and allocate credit fairly among GLP-1 identification, physiology, and therapeutic translation.",
      "Whether B045's VLP-centered discovery can be attributed to the proposed trio after separating it from papillomavirus carcinogenesis research, product development, and implementation."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No candidate-specific conflict is apparent from the supplied profile. My documented research in autoimmunity and rheumatology concerns related disease areas but does not establish a personal connection to Feldmann, Maini, or any other proposed candidate."
  }
}
